rces\nIndigent Defense Services Public Defender's Office\nHow-Tos\nInformation Technology\nManagement & Budget\nMedical Examiner\nOakland County Children's Village\nPay Taxes\nPretrial & Justice Services\nProperty Gateway\nProsecutor Conviction Integrity Unit\nCommunity\nTeen Court\nPurchasing Bidnet Registration\nG2G Marketplace\nRoads\nSheriff About Us\nOCSO Organization\nCommunity Services\nSurvey Oakland\nOakland County Treasurer's Office Property Taxes\nFinancial Empowerment Center\nVeterans Resources\nBenefits/Services\nWater Resources Commissioner Services\nHardship Assistance Program\nRainSmart Rebates\nG2G Cloud Solutions Accessibility\nFind Service\nTop Searches: Property Records • Inmate Locator\nFind Service\nGovernment\nClerk/Register of Deeds\nProperty & Land\nClerk/Register of Deeds\nAbout Us\nElections & Voting\nCourt Records\nProperty & Land\nCondo Exhibit B Plans\nFees & Forms\nMaps\nPlat Review\nProperty Fraud\nProperty Records\nRecording\nUnits\nLife Events & Services\n► View Subpages\nContact Info\nRegister of Deeds\n248-858-0597\ndeeds@ oaklandcountymi.gov\n1200 North Telegraph Road\nDept 480\nPontiac, MI 48341\nGet Email News & Updates\nCampus Map\nMonday – Friday\n8:30am - 4:30pm\nProperty & Land\nAs of 11/3/25 the Oakland County Register of Deeds no longer records UCC documents separately from land records. Accordingly, the recording fees for land records apply to UCC filings.\nOverview\nThe Register of Deeds Office creates a public record for all land situated in Oakland County. This includes deeds, mortgages, foreclosure records and personal property filings. By using Oakland County Super Index you can obtain copies of any recorded document(s) which date back to January 1, 1964, with the exception of subdivision plat maps.\nDocuments recorded with our office are scanned and microfilmed using the most modern methods to ensure safety and replacement at any time. Recorded documents are indexed and returned to the submitter in a prompt manner by U.S. Mail, unless otherwise noted.\nPlease note: The Register of Deeds office does not handle birth certificates, other vital records or UCC filings for transferring utilities.\nAn Important Message from Oakland County Clerk, Lisa Brown\nYour browser does not support inline frames. lt;br gt;\nlt;br gt;\nPlease visit lt;a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rJjr0qOflQU\" target=\"_blank\" gt;https://www.youtube.com/embed/rJjr0qOflQU lt;/a gt;\nOnline Services\nSuper Index\nProperty Records Notification (PRN)\nElectronic Recording\nContact Info\nRegister of Deeds\n248-858-0597\ndeeds@ oaklandcountymi.gov\n1200 North Telegraph Road\nDept 480\nPontiac, MI 48341\nGet Email News & Updates\nCampus Map\nMonday – Friday\n8:30am - 4:30pm\nContact Us\n1200 N. Telegraph Road\nPontiac, MI 48341\nCampus Map\nMain: 248-858-1000\nToll Free: 888-350-0900\nContact Us Form\nUseful Links\nDepartment Directory\nService Directory\nOakAlert\nPublic Meeting Notices\nWatch Commission Meetings\nCounty Budget\nInvestor Relations\nTransparency Dashboard\n.Gov Domain Transition\nConnect with Us\nEnter Email Address\nClick for More\nPrivacy/Legal | ADA Accessibility | HIPAA | Site Map | FOIA",
